course: dictionary
lesson: 11007
title: Being watchful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Watchful is an adjective. It describes someone who is paying careful attention to what is happening, so they notice any danger or problem. Look at the clues around it. «Real rabbits are not brave officers either: they are shy, watchful prey that hear danger early with their big ears and bolt before a fox gets close.» Rabbits hear danger early and run before a fox comes close, so watchful must mean alert and noticing danger.
explain: Watchful is often used with a parent, teacher or lifeguard who keeps an eye on children. A lifeguard is watchful when they stay alert to the swimmers and spot trouble at once. Ask yourself: is the person looking out for danger, or just resting? If they are looking out carefully, the word is watchful.
explain: Watchful often appears in set phrases: "under the watchful eye of", "keep a watchful eye on", and "stay watchful". Each one tells you someone is paying careful attention. Try swapping in "careful and alert" to check the meaning still fits.
fact: Watchful means paying careful attention to what is happening, so you notice any danger or problem.
fact: «Watchful» is an adjective, and its forms are watchful, more watchful and most watchful.
fact: A check is to swap in careful and alert: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Phrases to learn: "under the watchful eye of", "keep a watchful eye on", "stay watchful".
fact: Watchful is used in stories, safety and everyday life, and in stories it can suggest protection or suspicion.
exercise: «Real rabbits are not brave officers either: they are shy, watchful prey.» What does watchful mean here? | Sleepy and slow | *Paying careful attention to danger | Hungry all the time | Brave and loud
exercise: «A watchful lifeguard keeps an eye on the swimmers.» What does watchful suggest? | *Paying careful attention, so danger is noticed | Very angry with the swimmers | Not interested in anything at all | Asleep on the beach
exercise: Copy the word from «they are shy, watchful prey» that means paying careful attention. | officers | *watchful | rabbits | fox
test: «The guard kept a watchful eye on the gate all night.» What is the guard doing? | Shouting at the gate | Looking at the sky for birds | *Carefully watching for danger | Closing their eyes to sleep
test: Ella crossed the road under the watchful eye of her mum. What does watchful mean? | Asleep and unaware | Happy and singing | Tired and cross | *Alert, paying careful attention to danger
exam: Which sentence uses watchful correctly? | The cat was watchful because it was hungry for lunch. | The cat was watchful and fell fast asleep on the sofa all afternoon. | The cat was watchful of the sunny windowsill, purring and dreaming. | *The cat was watchful of the mouse hole, ready to spot any movement.
